ice and  you want to do well with your you have a  company of your own or you're working  for someone else you have to do that job  well that's the direct  objective that you have to achieve you  have to do that well in order to  achieve the sort of indirect  uh  you know  goal that will be the consequence of  your  commitment to doing the job well  or to making sure you have the skills  and the knowledge that you need in order  to achieve that longer term goal even in  personal relationships  you can't just go up to someone and say  i want to be your friend  or i want to be your lover  you first have to invest some time and  effort  into getting to know that person  giving that person a chance to get to  know you  uh they have to like you you have to  like them you know at that level you  build up  a connection  an emotional connection or a connection  of respect  which then  will eat the result the long-term but in  a way indirect result of that person and  you will become friends or lovers or  whatever the case may be  so  there's no sort of short circuit there's  no  you know jumping ahead of yourself you  have to first find that  short term  direct goal that you can focus on that's  going to lead you to your longer term  goal maybe i'm not making any sense here  when i bring it back to language  learning what this means is  you have to find something to like in  the language you're learning  if you cannot find anything to like  anything of interest you're going to  have a very tough time you can't just  say i would like to be fluent in english  because i need it for my job i would  like to be fluent in german or chinese  because it's going to be good for my  career  you actually have to find something  in chinese culture in german culture and  whatever japanese french russian  something that you like  you don't have to like everything  similarly it helps if you find a friend  but you don't have to like all chinese  russians japanese french you name it but  you 